WEBVTT

00:00:00.294 --> 00:00:01.254
I don't want to just do that.

00:00:01.254 --> 00:00:03.174
I want to understand
how this place works,

00:00:03.174 --> 00:00:05.894
right? Because that's my
entrepreneurship mind from what I learned

00:00:05.894 --> 00:00:09.350
here. But in a career, I wasn't
being taught any of that stuff.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.918
I was being taught
how to do my job well.

00:00:12.246 --> 00:00:13.286
So I had to sacrifice.

00:00:13.286 --> 00:00:16.406
I had to sacrifice time to go
and show up in these other places

00:00:16.406 --> 00:00:19.046
and learn how to be beneficial
to the creative director and not

00:00:19.046 --> 00:00:20.726
just my strategic boss, right?

00:00:20.726 --> 00:00:23.686
Or be beneficial to the CEO
or to these different people.

00:00:23.686 --> 00:00:26.246
And they would never
shun me out of the rooms,

00:00:26.246 --> 00:00:28.326
which let me know that I
probably should be there,

00:00:28.326 --> 00:00:31.750
right? If you can get in a room,
And you're allowed to be there,

00:00:31.750 --> 00:00:34.790
even if you don't have a role,
just listen and soak it up.

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:35.910
And that's what I used to do.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:38.230
And she used to call me worker
bee, and she didn't realize like

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:39.910
I wanted to run my own agency.

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.070
So I don't know, you could call
me whatever you want to call me,

00:00:42.070 --> 00:00:43.270
and y'all could work eight hours.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:45.830
I'll work 16-hour days until I
figure out how to make this work

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:48.982
for me. And it manifested
and it took a long time,

00:00:48.982 --> 00:00:50.082
but

00:00:50.246 --> 00:00:53.606
I was sacrificing. I was
sacrificing the time that my friends

00:00:53.606 --> 00:00:56.006
wouldn't, you know, for the things
that I felt like could benefit

00:00:56.006 --> 00:00:57.446
me because I just
had no clue, right?

00:00:57.446 --> 00:00:58.798
This was new to me.

00:00:59.062 --> 00:01:01.622
But it was something I had never
seen, and I had seen a lot.

00:01:01.622 --> 00:01:03.772
So I went this way.

00:01:04.022 --> 00:01:08.246
That's fair. That's a gem too for
y'all to like put in your back

00:01:08.246 --> 00:01:12.614
pocket is When you have
opportunities, this concept

00:01:12.614 --> 00:01:14.774
of like just remaining
curious, right?

00:01:14.774 --> 00:01:19.174
Like you may be there to do one
thing, but like keeping your eyes

00:01:19.174 --> 00:01:23.086
open, asking questions, like
being mindful about like.

00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:27.430
It doesn't have to end here,
I think, is a real key,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:28.846
I think, as part of like.

00:01:29.222 --> 00:01:33.222
Entrepreneurship and as part of
being like a founder and a visionary

00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:36.982
is really just being able to
like see a bigger picture outside

00:01:36.982 --> 00:01:39.142
of where you are and
just remain curious.

00:01:39.142 --> 00:01:40.822
And like, let me look
behind this door and like,

00:01:40.822 --> 00:01:41.942
what are y'all doing back there?

00:01:41.942 --> 00:01:43.302
Oh, okay, I really like that.

00:01:43.302 --> 00:01:44.422
How do I get more of that?

00:01:44.422 --> 00:01:48.262
Okay, that's cool. I want to go
now to see how this thing works.

00:01:48.262 --> 00:01:51.880
And so, just following that
trail of curiosity will lead you.

00:01:52.518 --> 00:01:53.376
So far.
